# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
#
# rcraid auto-bind rule
#
# AMD's chipset exposes EVERY downstream NVMe behind 0x1022:0xb000 — the
# array members and the drive carrying / alike.  On a box where all drives
# come from one OEM their subsystem_vendor is identical too, so matching on
# it (as this rule used to) protects nothing there and, worse, silently
# rebinds the OS drive: nvme is unbound, rcbottom probes the controller with
# CC.EN=0, no volume assembles, and pivot_root fails.  See issue #8.
#
# So the rule now fires on the namespace that nvme publishes, and
# rcraid-bind decides by reading the RAIDCore metadata at LBA 0x5000 — which
# firmware writes on members only.  The same read cannot disturb the device,
# so a non-member (including the root disk) is left bound to nvme.
#
# Firing on the block device rather than the PCI function also means the
# namespace exists by the time the helper runs, so the metadata is readable
# in an initramfs as well.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="disk", \
  KERNEL=="nvme[0-9]*n[0-9]", \
  ATTRS{vendor}=="0x1022", ATTRS{device}=="0xb000", \
  RUN+="/usr/sbin/rcraid-bind --disk /dev/%k"
